content.text:
Product has finished the copy, and I merged it into `docs/acceptance-criteria.md` (`cc1861f`).

- **New copy:** 9 new strings, added as entries C-24 to C-32. All match the designer's proposals except one reword:
  - the header, "Relay" and "Customer admin";
  - the footer heading and base line, "About these numbers" and "Relay · Activity health";
  - the "Week" label;
  - the picker's helper line and range line;
  - the table caption, "Locations — most unusual first".
- **New checks:** UI-46 to UI-49 cover the header and footer showing in every state, the picker only allowing Mondays in range, and using the picker by keyboard.
- **Updated entries:** six existing entries now reflect the redesign. The footnotes live in the footer, the week control is disabled but still visible for account 20, status is still never shown by colour alone, and so on.

**One reword to be aware of:** the week picker button's hidden screen-reader name is now "Mon Jul 20 – Sun Jul 26, 2026, choose week" rather than "Choose week, Mon Jul 20…". It follows the accessibility rule that the name should start with the text you can see on screen. It isn't shown anywhere, so it doesn't change the design you approved. Say so if you'd prefer the other order.

The architect is still running; it will add the redesign entry to PLAN.md §13. Once that lands I'll start frontend on the implementation.

Noted, and saved to memory. Until now I had been running installs and tests on main after merging, and the app is still running from the main checkout. From here on all of that happens inside the agents' own worktrees, and the main session only dispatches agents, merges their commits and reports to you.

**Where things stand:**
- Frontend's package setup is merged on main: Angular Material 22.2, the date-fns adapter, and self-hosted Geist.
- Error icon red: you said "Yes approved", which I've taken as keeping it as is, in the same red family as "Higher than usual". Tell me if you meant a different colour.
- Test-author is writing the failing tests in its own worktree. They cover:
  - the week picker: only Mondays in range can be picked, keyboard use, and the button's hidden name;
  - the header and footer in every state;
  - the footnotes sitting in the footer;
  - the table caption;
  - status never shown by colour alone;
  - account 20's week control disabled but still showing the week.

When it reports back I'll bring you the list of tests and the failing test output to review. Frontend won't start implementing until you've reviewed them.

